\section{Introduction and Document Scope}
%---------------------------------------------------------------

This chapter constitutes Part 5 of the Final Design Report for the Solift H-VTOL project, prepared in fulfilment of the Design for Manufacturability (DFM) course requirements. Its purpose is to consolidate all quantitative design targets, material specifications, interface definitions, environmental ratings, and applicable compliance standards into a single authoritative reference document.

The specifications presented herein are organised around eight thematic domains, each following an engineering data-sheet convention consistent with industrial practice (e.g., DJI Agras, Xag P100, Zipline Platform 2):

\begin{enumerate}
  \item Physical and Dimensional Parameters
  \item Propulsion and Electrical Systems
  \item Materials and Surface Treatments
  \item Structural and Mechanical Specifications
  \item Flight Performance and Operational Envelope
  \item Environmental and Survivability Specifications
  \item Avionics, Software, and Interface Standards
  \item Safety, Regulatory, and Compliance Standards
\end{enumerate}

