\subsection{Corrosion Protection Strategy}

Given the operational environment (outdoor logistics, salt-mist rated to IP54), a multi-layer corrosion protection strategy is mandated for all metallic parts:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{CFRP--Al interface:} All aluminium parts in contact with CFRP must be isolated with a glass-fibre fabric ply or PTFE tape to prevent galvanic corrosion ($\Delta E^\circ_{\text{CFRP--Al}} \approx 1.0\,\text{V}$).
  \item \textbf{Aluminium components:} Type III hard anodise per MIL-A-8625F, minimum coating thickness 25 \textmu m.
  \item \textbf{Steel fasteners:} Prohibited; replaced with TC4 titanium to eliminate galvanic couples.
  \item \textbf{Sealant:} PR-1422 polysulfide sealant applied to all wing/fuselage faying surfaces.
\end{enumerate}

