\subsection{Hover Performance}

The total required thrust margin in hover is calculated below to validate the motor selection:

\begin{align}
  T_{\text{required}} &= MTOW \times g = 12.0\,\text{kg} \times 9.81\,\text{m/s}^2 = 117.7\,\text{N} \\
  T_{\text{available}} &= 2 \times T_{\text{front}} + 1 \times T_{\text{rear}} \nonumber \\
                       &= 2 \times 44.1\,\text{N} + 53.9\,\text{N} = 142.1\,\text{N} \\
  \text{Thrust Margin} &= \frac{T_{\text{available}} - T_{\text{required}}}{T_{\text{required}}} \times 100\%
                       = \frac{142.1 - 117.7}{117.7} \times 100\% = \mathbf{20.7\%}
\end{align}

A thrust margin of $\geq$20\% is the minimum required to accommodate wind gusts and dynamic manoeuvres without saturation. The Solift design achieves exactly this threshold.

