\subsection{Safety-Critical Design Requirements}

The following design requirements are classified as \textbf{safety-critical} and may not be waived without formal engineering authority approval:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{SR-01:} All propulsion motors must maintain independent power paths. No single wiring failure shall disable more than one motor.
  \item \textbf{SR-02:} The battery management system (BMS) shall interrupt power within 50 ms of detecting cell voltage below 3.3 V or cell temperature above 75\textdegree C.
  \item \textbf{SR-03:} The tilt mechanism pivot shaft shall be designed with a structural safety factor $\geq$ 1.5 against ultimate load under worst-case transition phase gyroscopic loading (verified by FEA).
  \item \textbf{SR-04:} A geofence enforced at firmware level shall prevent flight beyond pre-loaded boundaries. Fence breach shall trigger immediate RTH.
  \item \textbf{SR-05:} All structural CFRP--aluminium interfaces shall be galvanically isolated per Section~\ref{sec:corrosion} to prevent stress-corrosion cracking.
  \item \textbf{SR-06:} The platform shall achieve failsafe RTH within 1 second of RC link loss, confirmed by hardware-in-the-loop (HITL) simulation prior to any flight test.
\end{enumerate}

